1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,122
Cowboys versus Wizards lets card players test a balance change before it hits their deck.

2
00:00:06,152 --> 00:00:10,554
Billy breaks Bone Wall. Kiro wants to take one point off that shot.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:16,506
Try the shot again. Same Billy, same wall. This time it survives with one orb.

4
00:00:16,536 --> 00:00:20,448
Let the bots play on, and the Wizards win on turn twenty.

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:26,074
But you can take Billy’s next turn. The Headless Horseman is right in front of him.

6
00:00:26,104 --> 00:00:29,485
Shoot, and the Wizards still win. Two turns sooner.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:35,815
Back up to that same turn and take cover. Now the Cowboys win on turn twenty-one.

8
00:00:35,845 --> 00:00:38,094
The weaker Billy still had a way out.

9
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,944
That shot began in a Kiro workflow. One agent could change one number on one card.

10
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:53,574
A separate reviewer used this spec. Each faction had to win between forty-five and fifty-five percent of the bot games.

11
00:00:54,280 --> 00:01:00,738
We tested twenty-five thousand unseen deals, from both seats, with both versions of Billy.

12
00:01:00,768 --> 00:01:10,748
Across a hundred thousand bot duels, Cowboy wins fell from fifty-nine point eight percent to fifty-one point nine. The first player still had an edge.

13
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:19,806
Billy still hits for two on the Trail. At the Night Shift Saloon, you can play the proposed change before it ever reaches your deck.
